.TH CHECK_STATUS.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "otsdaq-mu2e 11.03.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
check_status.sh \- run git fetch, git status and git remote in each otsdaq
source directory of an MRB development area
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sh check_status.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Despite its name,
.B check_status.sh
does not check hardware or DAQ status.
It is a source-tree status sweep from the MRB/UPS era.
Run it from the
.I srcs/
directory of an MRB development area.
It enters each of these eleven directories in turn and runs
.BR "git fetch" ,
.B git status
and
.BR "git remote \-v" :
.PP
.EX
mu2e_pcie_utils  otsdaq_components  otsdaq  otsdaq_utilities
otsdaq_mu2e_calorimeter  otsdaq_mu2e_trigger  otsdaq_mu2e
otsdaq_mu2e_crv  otsdaq_mu2e_extmon  otsdaq_mu2e_stm  otsdaq_mu2e_tracker
.EE
.PP
The names use underscores.
Spack development areas use hyphenated names such as
.IR otsdaq\-mu2e .
.B git fetch
contacts every remote and can prompt for credentials.
.PP
The file has no
.B #!
line and is not installed on the
.BR PATH .
.SH OPTIONS
None.
Arguments are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status of the final
.BR cd ,
normally 0.
Failures of
.B git
are not reported in the exit status.
.SH CAVEATS
A failed
.B cd
is not detected.
For every directory that is missing, the
.B git
commands run in the starting directory instead.
In a Spack area, the sweep therefore reports the same repository (or "not a
git repository") eleven times.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
cd $MRB_SOURCE && sh /path/to/otsdaq\-mu2e/tools/check_status.sh
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR check_firmware_version.sh (1)
(for DTC firmware),
.BR otsdaq-mu2e-tools (7)
